<title>UK: Dollar, Chicago boost UK meals and feeds prices.</title>
<headline>Dollar, Chicago boost UK meals and feeds prices.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK meals and feeds prices surged on Monday on reports of low rainfall in the U.S. Midwest and the firmer dollar.</p>
<p>High protein soymeal was as much as six stg up ex-mill while stores were up to 4.50 stg higher.</p>
<p>Rapemeal ex-mill Erith was two stg up while Liverpool and Hull prices were four stg higher.</p>
<p>Corn gluten feed pellets were one stg up while sunflower meals and pellets were unchanged.</p>
<p>--Jim Ballantyne, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8062</p>
</text>
